        '3-5', $q$A Weather Station for Our School$q$, $q$(1) Every morning, our class checks the weather on a tablet before recess. (2) I believe our school should build its own weather station on the roof of the gym. (3) First, a weather station would make science lessons more real. (4) Students could measure rainfall, wind speed, and temperature every day. (5) Specifically, our fifth grade weather unit asks us to graph data for two weeks. (6) Right now, we copy numbers from a website instead of collecting them ourselves.

(7) ______ a weather station would help the whole school stay safe. (8) The office could check the wind speed before deciding whether recess should be held outside. (9) Last spring, a strong gust knocked over the soccer goals while students were playing nearby. (10) My cousin lives in a town where it snows almost every winter.

(11) Some families may worry about the cost. (12) A basic weather station costs about the same as two new classroom rugs, and the parent club has already offered to help pay for it.$q$, 'draft')
