        '3-5', $q$A Trip to the Old Canal$q$, $q$(1) Each year, the fifth grade takes a field trip to the city aquarium. (2) This year, we should visit the old canal and its lock house instead. (3) The canal connects directly to what we study in social studies. (4) In class, we are learning how goods moved from farms to cities before there were trains. (5) At the canal, guides show how mules pulled flat boats along a path beside the water. (6) Seeing the real locks fill with water would help us understand how boats climbed hills.

(7) The canal trip would also save money. (8) The canal park is only twenty minutes from school, while the aquarium is almost two hours away. (9) ______ the bus would cost less, and we would have more time to explore. (10) The lock house tour is free for school groups on weekdays.

(11) The aquarium is fun, but we already visited it when we were in third grade. (12) A canal trip would teach us something new.$q$, 'draft')
