   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence before sentence (3) to introduce the first reason. Which sentence works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some students like to play in the bright sun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposing-idea-as-topic"},{"text":"First, trees would protect students from the heat.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Trees can live for more than one hundred years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-a-reason"},{"text":"In conclusion, shade is important for everyone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-conclusion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$First, trees would protect students from the heat.$q$, $q$Sentences (3) to (5) are all about heat, so a sentence naming heat as the first reason introduces them clearly. The fact about how long trees live is true but does not name the reason those sentences support.$q$, 'draft', '4b8500d6-3c0e-5943-aba1-daf6d49d0bd6')
