        '3-5', $q$Typing Lessons for Fifth Grade$q$, $q$(1) Students in our school use laptops for reports, quizzes, and research. (2) However, no one ever teaches us how to type correctly. (3) Our school should add short typing lessons to fifth grade computer class. (4) Typing well saves time. (5) A student who types with all ten fingers can usually finish a page much faster than a student who uses two fingers. (6) Last month, my partner Priya typed our whole science report while I was still typing the title.

(7) Typing lessons would also help students do better on tests. (8) Many of our state tests are now taken on computers. (9) ______ students who type slowly may run out of time before they finish writing their answers. (10) Computers were once so large that they filled an entire room.

(11) Some teachers worry that typing lessons would take time away from other subjects. (12) The lessons could last only ten minutes at the start of each computer class.$q$, 'draft')
