  ('d2b06dbf-dec2-562a-b77d-35b98c584761', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-opinion-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence (5) uses the word "usually." Why is this a good choice in an opinion piece?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It links the reason to the teachers' worry in sentence (11).","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-link"},{"text":"It keeps the claim accurate, since not every ten-finger typist is faster.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It turns the detail into a conclusion for the whole draft.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail-with-conclusion"},{"text":"It shows the writer is not sure about the opinion in sentence (3).","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-hedge-as-doubt"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It keeps the claim accurate, since not every ten-finger typist is faster.$q$, $q$"Usually" makes the claim true for most students without claiming it is true for everyone, which keeps the support believable. It does not mean the writer doubts the opinion, which is stated firmly in sentence (3).$q$, 'draft', 'ae52be65-58e1-5f4b-8128-d0714b704ae6')
