   $q$After the writer removes the sentence that does not belong, which concluding statement would best end the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"White socks can turn pink when washed with red clothes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-conclusion"},{"text":"Chores are the only way for kids to learn anything useful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"},{"text":"Since chores build responsibility and teach real skills, families should give kids jobs at home.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Kids who play sports often have very busy afternoons.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ends-with-opposing-idea"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Since chores build responsibility and teach real skills, families should give kids jobs at home.$q$, $q$The correct choice restates the opinion and both reasons, responsibility and life skills. Saying chores are the only way to learn anything useful is an overstated claim that the draft does not support.$q$, 'draft', '7ee0fca5-b698-5680-81f7-21dc5c143725')
