  ('13e6f5d1-cd3c-513f-8acf-2036640411c1', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-opinion-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence (12) gives a new reason at the very end of the draft. What is the best way to revise it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Delete it, because saving money has nothing to do with the opinion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"Move it after sentence (9) as a new reason and add a fact about the cost.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Leave it at the end, because a new reason makes a strong ending.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-reason-as-conclusion"},{"text":"Move it before sentence (2) so that it becomes the opinion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-reason-with-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Move it after sentence (9) as a new reason and add a fact about the cost.$q$, $q$Saving money does support turning off lights, so it belongs with the other reasons, backed by a fact, before the response to the worry. A concluding statement should sum up reasons, not introduce a new one.$q$, 'draft', '061b9956-5948-519f-b6d4-00097d602450')
